From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 07:40:28 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: port the vendor 6.18 overlay changes

The Airoha 6.18 feed (airoha_openwrt_feeds_update_6.18, c287d2d81216)
forked its overlay sources before the 2026-08-07 feed release that the
files/ overlay follows. A verbatim copy of its sources reverts that
release, so the changes the vendor made on the 6.18 branch are carried
here as a patch and files/ stays identical to the 2026-08-07 release.

The l2b bridge bind fix and the NPU flow statistics patch that follow
in the series expect these changes.

Not ported, because no code in the vendor feed or in this tree sets
the flag: the IFF_PON_DEV test in airoha_ppe_is_pon_dev(). With that
test the function reports no PON device at all. Also not ported: the
weak dynamic_ifc_sock_in_use_hook definition in arht_wifi_lo.c, which
assumes arht_dynamic_ifc.c is not built, and it is built here. Also
not ported: the packet_hash_collision_check() rewrite. It removes one
VLAN tag only and reports no collision when a header pull fails, so a
frame with two tags is bound without an address compare.

Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
